prompt:
  text: "UX design sheet for the SemText `<sem-reveal>` element — the Q→A DISCLOSURE:\
    \ a question in a small-caps disclosure bar whose answer expands beneath it,\
    \ backed by native `<details>/<summary>`. FIVE stacked example pages, each\
    \ inside a browser-chrome frame with a small mono uppercase caption, rendered\
    \ in the minimal-tech theme on a dark slate canvas (bg #0f172a, surface\
    \ #1e293b, fg #e2e8f0, hairline #334155 borders, 12px card radius). A reveal\
    \ is one card: 1px hairline border, rounded 12px, and inside it a disclosure\
    \ row — a small muted triangle marker, then the question in semibold — with\
    \ the answer prose underneath when open.\n\nPage 1 — caption \"COLLAPSED\".\
    \ One closed reveal card, question \"Why not localStorage?\", the row in\
    \ semibold with a small right-pointing triangle before it, NO answer prose\
    \ visible, NO second copy of the question anywhere on the card — the\
    \ disclosure row is the only place the question appears.\n\nPage 2 — caption\
    \ \"OPEN\". The same card expanded: triangle rotated downward, the question\
    \ row unchanged, and the answer as ordinary readable prose below the row\
    \ inside the same card (\"Tokens in localStorage are readable by any script\
    \ on the page — keep tokens in httpOnly cookies or memory only.\"). Nothing\
    \ overlaps; the card grows to fit.\n\nPage 3 — caption \"DERIVED SUMMARY\".\
    \ A closed reveal whose question was never authored: the bar reads the\
    \ opening words of the answer (\"Why derive the label at all? Because the\
    \ summary a reader…\") cut at a word boundary, showing that the label is\
    \ derived from the body text. The cut is mid-sentence by design; do not\
    \ complete the sentence.\n\nPage 4 — caption \"CLASS FORM\". Two reveal\
    \ cards side by side, identical in size and styling: left one labeled with a\
    \ tiny mono chip \"<sem-reveal summary>\" above it, right one labeled\
    \ \"<div class=sem-reveal data-summary>\". Both show the same closed question\
    \ \"Why not localStorage?\" — the two spellings must look exactly alike.\n\n\
    Page 5 — caption \"NO SCRIPT\". One reveal as it reads with JavaScript\
    \ unavailable: NO triangle, NO disclosure bar, NO interactivity chrome — the\
    \ question as a small-caps muted heading line, then the full answer as plain\
    \ prose, all fully visible. The whole answer shows; nothing is hidden, and\
    \ no control affordance is drawn.\n\nTypography: clean system sans\
    \ (Inter-like), 16px body, 1.6 line height, generous margins, mono uppercase\
    \ captions. The accent color appears only on the triangle markers and focus\
    \ affordances; the question rows stay fg-colored. No icons, no emoji, no\
    \ extra buttons.\n"
  negative: 'the question rendered twice on one card (small-caps caption above the
    disclosure bar AND again inside it); answer text visible on a closed card; answer
    text occluded, blurred, struck through or drawn as a redaction bar; reveals drawn
    as modals, tooltips, popovers, toast notifications, accordions with plus/minus
    icons or speech bubbles; the no-script page showing a control affordance, triangle
    or hidden content; the derived-summary page showing a completed sentence; neon
    glow; drop shadows on text; light background; more or fewer than five example
    pages; watermark; lorem ipsum in captions.

    '
  style: 'Flat UI spec sheet, minimal-tech aesthetic, restrained palette — hairline
    #334155 borders, 12px card radius, generous negative space; the only color is
    the small accent triangle and the focus affordance. Looks like a panel from a
    design-system guide.

    '
